    "result_text": "All 289 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When creating an owner, it's set to `true` if another owner already has the same address **and** city, otherwise `false`. Creation is still always allowed.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `sharesHousehold` field (`@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 set the flag via a new `sharesHousehold(owner)` helper that checks existing owners for a matching address + city, before saving.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column so the persisted flag survives to the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read.\n\nMapStruct maps the field automatically by name, so no mapper change was needed. The flag is computed against the resolved city (after the existing canonical-spelling normalization) and persisted, matching the \"set in the owner response at creation\" semantics the test verifies via a follow-up GET.",
